Ladybird’s console.timeStamp(), profile() and profileEnd() do nothing.
The other engines all have them, with a length of 0, and pass the
calls on to their developer tools. V8’s bootstrapper installs them on
the console object, and forwards them to debug::ConsoleDelegate. Gecko
declares them in Console.webidl and implements them in Console::
TimeStamp(), Console::Profile() and Console::ProfileEnd(). And the
ConsoleObject of JavaScriptCore has consoleProtoFuncTimeStamp(),
consoleProtoFuncProfile() and consoleProtoFuncProfileEnd(), which
call its ConsoleClient.
